{"ts":"2026-09-25T19:22:21.091Z","author":"pilot:claude-sonnet-5@claude-anthropic-harness","name":"log/20260925T192147Z/000050","body":"All four steps ran. Steps 3 and 4 were refused, as the bounds say they should be.\n\n1. **`safe_probe.py` with args `one two`** ran with exit code 0 in 54 ms. Its output is in `[[log/20260925T192147Z/000024]]`.\n   - It reported Python 3.13.3 in isolated mode, with UTF-8 mode on.\n   - The working directory was the workspace, and the args came through as `['one','two']`.\n   - The environment had only four keys: SYSTEMROOT, TEMP, TMP and WINDIR.\n   - Unicode printed correctly.\n   - The script wrote \"safe_probe: done\" to stderr as normal output, not as an error.\n2. **Draft and workspace copy.**\n   - I wrote ledger entry `pilot/phase1/hello_draft` (id `20260925T192147Z:89`). Its body is a shebang line plus `print(\"hello\")`, which is two lines.\n   - `mcp__fs__write` copied it to `workspace/hello_draft.py` (38 bytes, sha256 `c5b5f9cd…7ee75`; record `[[log/20260925T192147Z/000035]]`).\n3. **Running the workspace copy** was denied: \"outside this agent's fs.exec (…/scripts)\". The workspace is in `fs.write` and only the scripts directory is in `fs.exec`, so the copy can't be run until a human promotes it.\n4. **Writing the same entry into `scripts/hello_draft.py`** was denied: \"in the harness scripts directory, which no agent may write; a human promotes scripts\".\n\n**Observed:**\n- The two refusals had clear messages that named the rule.\n- Reading onboarding v1.12 was the only read I did. It says harnesses may be variants with modified toolsets, which matches what I saw.\n\n**Not observed:**\n- Neither refusal seemed to produce a ledger record that I could see, and I didn't check the `log/` entries for them.\n- I didn't verify the file contents on disk after writing.\n\n**Inferred:** the isolated-run and permission checks are enforced before the script starts, not inside it.\n\n**Nothing malformed** in the instructions or tools. One small mismatch: the CLI environment block names PowerShell and Bash, but I have neither, which the prompt anticipated.\n\n`hello_draft.py` in the workspace is ready for human review and promotion."}
